# WACV artifact: the PRIVATE half. This repository is public (every notebook
# clones it with no credentials), and these two files hold gated FERMAT text
# and the second-rater blinding key. The artifact's own README says they are
# excluded from release, so committing them here would contradict it.
reference/wacv_evaluation_artifact/fermat_n300_private_manifest.csv
reference/wacv_evaluation_artifact/second_rater_blinding_key_PRIVATE.csv

# GATED DATASET TEXT -- must not be in a public release.
# FERMAT is gated (ai4bharat/FERMAT, gated=auto) and these run CSVs carry its
# `orig_q` and `pert_a` verbatim, plus raw generations derived from gated
# pages. 19 such files, ~26 MB, were tracked here from 5ebc218 onward; the
# CLAUDE.md note claiming `results/` was untracked was simply wrong. Untracked
# 2026-08-15 before submission. Local copies are untouched: only the public
# release changes. The releasable substitute is
# reference/wacv_evaluation_artifact/fermat_n300_public_manifest.csv, which
# carries ids, hashes and derived numbers but no gated text.
results/
.dryrun_scratch/

# Figure 2 source pages: gated FERMAT content, same reason as results/ above.
# The composed figure (paper/figures/four_quadrant.png) IS committed, as any
# paper figure of a dataset must be; the unrendered pages are not. Export with
# pilot/31_export_figure2_pages.ipynb -- see paper/figures/pages/README.md.
paper/figures/pages/*.jpg

# The paper itself is not published here. WACV is double-blind and main.pdf
# carries the author block, so a public repo of it is a deanonymisation risk.
# Local files are untouched; the paper lives in Overleaf.
paper/
